Read sig_ratio first. Pinned at the lower clip => the feedback loop ran the wrong way
(zero signal shrinks sigma, which makes ties more likely). Pinned at the upper clip =>
the gain is too high for the clip. Only a ratio that moves inside the band is a real test.

Caveats: alpha is fixed but effective_lr = alpha*sigma_t is not, so radius and step size
are confounded; 2 seeds; absolute accuracies now use the fixed extractor and are NOT
comparable to anything produced before 2026-08-10.
